Text:
    The determinant converts matrix multiplication into scalar multiplication.
    The explanation is published prose; it introduces no hidden assumptions.

/-- Multiplicativity for complex square matrices. -/
Result determinant product:
    Attribution: mathlib; Matrix.det_mul; specialized
    Let n: Natural
    Let A, B: Matrix(n,n,Complex)
    Conclude: det(A*B) = det(A)*det(B)

Text latex:
    \subsection{Reversing the order}
    Since scalar multiplication commutes, the two products $AB$ and $BA$
    have the same determinant.

Result determinant product swap:
    Attribution: mathlib; Matrix.det_mul_comm; specialized
    Let n: Natural
    Let A, B: Matrix(n,n,Complex)
    Conclude: det(A*B) = det(B*A)

